   "mechanisms": {
    "fridge_distractor_objects": "The policy relies on the fridge being a clean, unambiguous cooling target: it opens the fridge, sees only cup/plate/potato/tomato, and immediately knows 'cool mug with fridge' is available. This intervention injects distractor objects into the fridge observation so the fridge contents are crowded with irrelevant items, forcing the policy to reason about which object is the mug and whether the fridge is still the right cooler.",
    "fridge_open_requires_cooling_check": "The policy depends on the direct affordance 'cool mug 1 with fridge 1' appearing immediately once the mug is held and the fridge is open. This intervention delays/blocks that affordance until the policy has re-examined the fridge, breaking the shortcut of going straight from 'take mug' to 'cool mug with fridge' without confirming the fridge is still the correct cooler."
   },
